  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in North Berwick and East Lothian" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in North Berwick</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in North Berwick</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across North Berwick, East Lothian, and the wider EH39 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining North Berwick provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across North Berwick (EH39), East Lothian, and the wider area. Experienced with coastal properties, holiday let conversions, and commercial refurbishments along the East Lothian coast.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in North Berwick</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">North Berwick is a picturesque coastal town in East Lothian, situated approximately 12 miles east of Edinburgh city centre on the Firth of Forth. The EH39 postcode covers the historic town centre with its distinctive Georgian and Victorian architecture along the High Street, the Bass Rock visible on the horizon, and surrounding residential and coastal areas. North Berwick has a population of around 8,500 and is one of East Lothian's most popular destinations for tourists, second-home buyers, and retirees. The town's coastal location means a significant proportion of properties are used as holiday lets or second homes, creating steady demand for refurbishment drylining services. As a popular Edinburgh commuter town, North Berwick has also seen growth in residential refurbishment and conversion projects, particularly in the conversion of period properties into modern living spaces.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The area offers a distinctive mix of projects for our drylining team — from the careful internal refurbishment of period coastal properties to conversion works for holiday let and B&B properties. We cover the entire EH39 postcode and surrounding East Lothian areas, serving everything from single-room domestic projects in period cottages to larger commercial fit-outs along the town centre and waterfront. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards compliant with all relevant sections, with particular attention to moisture management and thermal performance in coastal locations.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in North Berwick</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our North Berwick crew handles everything from period coastal property refurbishments to holiday let conversions — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems across the EH39 postcode and East Lothian.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Period property drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in North Berwick's listed Georgian and Victorian coastal properties</li> <li><strong>Holiday let conversions</strong> — Full internal refurbishment drylining for holiday let and B&B properties, including fire-rated compartmentation compliant with Scottish Building Standards</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, hospitality venues, and cafe conversions along North Berwick High Street and the waterfront</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings requiring Scottish Building Standards Section 2 (Fire) compliance</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Commercial premises, offices, and residential properties across East Lothian coastal areas</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential properties, holiday lets, and mixed-use developments in North Berwick and surrounding East Lothian areas</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of North Berwick We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>North Berwick town centre (EH39) — High Street, South Street, West Port</li> <li>East Berwick and the Esplanade</li> <li>Gribben Head and Bass Rock Road area</li> <li>West Berwick and Harbour area</li> <li>Lothian Rise and residential estates (EH39)</li> <li>East Lothian coastal villages generally</li> <li>Haddington (EH41) — 15 minutes via A198</li> <li>Dirleton — 5 minutes via B6350</li> <li>Gifford — 10 minutes via B6350</li> <li>Eyre Street Beach and Gullane area</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">North Berwick Building Regulations &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">North Berwick falls under <strong>East Lothian Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The town centre contains numerous Category A, B, and C listed buildings, particularly properties along the High Street and waterfront that are within conservation areas. Many period properties are also within the <strong>North Berwick Conservation Area</strong>, meaning internal structural alterations may require additional consent. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council's building standards department to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a period coastal property to a commercial conversion — is fully compliant with Scottish Building Standards and any additional conservation requirements. Special attention is given to moisture management and thermal performance in coastal locations.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for North Berwick Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As an Edinburgh-based drylining team, we have extensive experience working across East Lothian, including North Berwick, Haddington, and the wider coastal villages. We understand the unique character of North Berwick — from its distinctive coastal properties and period architecture to the specific requirements of working with holiday lets and second homes. Our crew is familiar with Scottish Building Standards and the particular moisture and thermal challenges of working on coastal properties. Whether you need drylining for a period property conversion, a holiday let refurbishment, or a commercial fit-out, our team delivers quality work on time and within budget.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 